  "biography": {
    "narrative": "Miriam Rachel Cohen is an Israeli-American cognitive scientist and AI researcher born in Tel Aviv. She grew up in the Florentin neighbourhood and went on to complete her PhD at MIT before joining Google DeepMind in London. She returned to Israel in 2017 as an Associate Professor at Tel Aviv University, drawn back by the academic appointment and by a deep attachment to the city itself — the light, the pace, the market near her childhood home. She is internationally recognized for her work on human-AI interaction. Outside the lab she reads widely, plays piano, cycles on weekends, and follows Maccabi Tel Aviv basketball with entirely too much emotional investment.",
